id: pm-vcs-48q3
title: Per-field record merge so structured data never line-merges
description: "The reason the VCS exists. A record merge compares base, ours and theirs field by field: a field only one side changed takes that side, a field both sides changed to the same value is not a conflict, append-only sequences union while preserving order, and set-valued fields union. Only a genuine scalar disagreement conflicts, and it conflicts on that field alone rather than poisoning the whole document."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[1]: "area:vcs"
created_at: "2026-07-30T22:37:54.424Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-30T22:55:29.763Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: "Two agents editing different fields of one record merge cleanly; identical concurrent edits do not conflict; append-only history from both sides unions with no loss and no duplication; a real scalar disagreement reports exactly the conflicting field with base, ours and theirs; no record merge path can emit line-based conflict markers"
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
